DOCUMENT 1: PRODUCT REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT (PRD)
1.1 Feature Overview

Reconcile is a net-new feature for the CareIndeed Home Health platform that provides a centralized view for matching, validating, and closing gaps between required compliance/regulatory tasks and their actual completion status across the organization.

It answers the critical question: "For a given compliance period, what was required, what was done, what's missing, and what needs immediate action?"

1.2 Problem Statement

Currently, compliance officers and administrators must manually cross-reference multiple areas of the platform (CES, Evidence Locker, Policy Lifecycle, Clinician Profiles) to determine whether all regulatory obligations have been fulfilled. There is no single view that:

Aggregates all required compliance deliverables for a given period
Matches each requirement against submitted evidence/artifacts
Surfaces gaps, mismatches, and expired items
Tracks reconciliation progress toward audit-readiness
Provides exportable reconciliation reports for surveyors
1.3 Users & Personas
Persona	Role	Primary Use
Compliance Officer	Primary user	Runs reconciliation cycles, reviews gaps, assigns remediation
Agency Administrator	Oversight	Reviews reconciliation summaries, signs off on closure
Clinician	Contributor	Sees assigned remediation tasks from reconciliation
Brad AI Copilot	Automated assist	Surfaces anomalies, suggests matches, flags risks
1.4 Core Capabilities
#	Capability	Description
RC-01	Reconciliation Cycles	Create, manage, and close time-bound reconciliation periods (monthly, quarterly, annual, survey-prep)
RC-02	Requirement Ingestion	Automatically pull all compliance requirements from Taxonomy, Policy Lifecycle, CES, and Onboarding
RC-03	Evidence Matching	Match submitted evidence (from Evidence Locker) against each requirement — auto-match where possible, manual match for exceptions
RC-04	Gap Analysis	Identify requirements with no matching evidence, expired evidence, or partial completion
RC-05	Remediation Tracking	Assign gaps to responsible parties with due dates; track progress to closure
RC-06	Reconciliation Dashboard	Summary view showing cycle progress, match rates, gap counts, risk score
RC-07	Audit Export	Generate reconciliation reports in PDF format for surveyor presentation
RC-08	Brad AI Integration	AI-powered anomaly detection, auto-match suggestions, and natural language querying of reconciliation status
1.5 Success Metrics
Metric	Target
Time to complete quarterly reconciliation	Reduced from ~40 hours → ~8 hours
Gap identification accuracy	≥ 95% auto-detection rate
Evidence auto-match rate	≥ 80% for structured artifacts
Audit-readiness confidence score	Visible per cycle, target ≥ 90%
1.6 Out of Scope (V1)
Billing/financial reconciliation
EVV (Electronic Visit Verification) reconciliation
Payroll/staffing hours reconciliation
External system integrations (will use internal CES/Evidence/Policy data only)
