US-RC-002: View Reconciliation Dashboard

As a Compliance Officer, I want to see a summary dashboard for an active cycle, so I can quickly assess overall reconciliation health.

Acceptance Criteria:

 Shows: match rate %, gap count, critical gap count, risk score, audit-readiness status
 Shows breakdown by domain (Clinical, Safety, Compliance, etc.)
 Shows breakdown by source (CES, Policy, Taxonomy, Onboarding)
 Shows progress over time (line chart of match rate by day)
 One-click access to unmatched/gap items

US-RC-003: Auto-Match Evidence

As a Compliance Officer, I want the system to automatically match evidence from the Evidence Locker against requirements, so I don't have to manually find every document.

Acceptance Criteria:

 System runs auto-match when cycle moves from Draft → In-Progress
 Matches based on: requirement code in filename/metadata, date range overlap, domain match, clinician match
 Each auto-match has a confidence score (0-100)
 Auto-matches ≥ 85% confidence are marked "auto-matched"
 Auto-matches 50-84% are flagged for human review
 Auto-matches < 50% remain "unmatched"

US-RC-004: Manual Match Evidence

As a Compliance Officer, I want to manually match evidence to a requirement when auto-match doesn't find a result, so I can close gaps.

Acceptance Criteria:

 Can search Evidence Locker from within the line item view
 Can drag-and-drop or select evidence files to match
 Status changes to "manual-matched"
 Match is attributed to the user

US-RC-005: Review & Resolve Gaps

As a Compliance Officer, I want to review all unmatched requirements, assign remediation, or waive items with justification.

Acceptance Criteria:

 Gap list filterable by severity, domain, source, assignee
 Can assign remediation to a clinician/staff with due date
 Can waive a requirement with mandatory justification note
 Can dispute a requirement (escalates for review)
 Remediation tasks appear on the assignee's My Planner view

US-RC-006: Close a Reconciliation Cycle

As an Agency Administrator, I want to close a completed reconciliation cycle, confirming all items are addressed.

Acceptance Criteria:

 Cannot close if critical gaps remain unresolved
 Closing generates a timestamped reconciliation report
 Closed cycles are read-only
 Closure requires admin-level permission

US-RC-007: Export Reconciliation Report

As a Compliance Officer, I want to export a reconciliation report as PDF for surveyor presentation.

Acceptance Criteria:

 Report includes: cycle summary, all line items with match status, gap analysis, remediation log
 Report branded with CareIndeed header
 Exportable at any point during the cycle (watermarked "DRAFT" if not closed)

US-RC-008: Brad AI Reconciliation Assistant

As a Compliance Officer, I want to ask Brad AI questions about reconciliation status in natural language.

